-- =========================================================================
-- SetExpr + SetPattern + their payload types — the canonical $variant /
-- $record entity ADTs the set-algebra-to-fenel migration targets.
-- Phase 1 (brief:
-- `workstreams/set-algebra-to-fenel/briefs/phase-1-register-setexpr-pattern-entities.md`).
--
-- Floor-kernel Phase 4 (2026-07-11) completed the representation convergence:
-- this registered ADT (15-case since signature-substrate P4 slice 3a added
-- SeRigid) is the sole internal SetExpr. TypeScript declares
-- the matching mandatory host value shape; exact legacy `$`-key values are read
-- only as `unknown` by the structural boundary and are never a second SetExpr
-- type. Persisted producers/readers normalize to this form.
--
-- NAMING — the `Set`-prefixed family (Rom decision 2026-06-16, brief Option 1).
-- The brief's locked D1 names `Pattern` / `Interval` / `Bound` all COLLIDE with
-- already-registered catalog entities, so they are disambiguated here:
--   • `Pattern`  is taken by `fenel/std/expr.fenel` — the expr-substrate
--     MATCH-ARM ADT (PatLit | PatVar | PatWildcard | PatConstruct), an unrelated
--     concept. The set-algebra regex/sequence pattern is `SetPattern`.
--   • `Interval` / `Bound` are taken by the exact tagged internal shapes the
--     deciders declare module-local (`BoundNumber | BoundString | BoundExpr`
--     and `Interval (Maybe Bound) (Maybe Bound)`). They leak to the global
--     catalog through the engine module. The host-canonical SeInterval payload
--     remains an untagged structural record; classify/declassify functions are
--     its explicit boundary to the tagged internal algebra.
-- The SetExpr/SetPattern CASE names use distinct Se* / Sp* / Bv* families —
-- only the colliding ENTITY names take the `Set` prefix.
--
-- MODELING NOTES (faithful to `types.ts`, with two documented divergences from
-- the brief's literal field-type text, both forced by "no registered entity"):
--   • `SeWhere pred` + `BvExpr expr` — the brief writes `Expression` (D3:
--     `$where` carries JSON-Logic, NOT the `Expr` ADT). There is NO registered
--     `Expression` entity (`Expr` exists but is the IR core ADT — the WRONG
--     concept per D3), so the JSON-Logic payload is explicitly `Any`. Phase 2b
--     routes `$where` through `evaluateWith`; it does NOT retype this slot (the
--     `Expr`-ADT-typed `$where` is expr-substrate's tail).
--   • `SeEnum values` — the brief writes `List Json`; `types.ts` is `unknown[]`.
--     No registered `Json` entity, so the finite value set is `List Any`,
--     mirroring `unknown[]` without manufacturing a declaration-local generic.
--     SetExpr remains the ground, non-parametric type used throughout the host
--     algebra; Phase 2 schemes live above it rather than turning it into a type
--     constructor.
--   • `SetBound` / `SetInterval` are single-constructor records whose
--     constructor name = the type name (the `Int = Int …` idiom) — deliberately
--     NOT a bare `Bound` / `Interval` constructor, to keep the constructor
--     namespace clear of the deciders' marshalled types.
--
-- MUTUAL RECURSION: `SetExpr.SePattern : SetPattern` and `SetPattern.SpMatch :
-- SetExpr` (+ `SpGroup.type : Maybe SetExpr`) cross-reference. Both register in
-- the same load pass (`type-foundation.ts`'s line-920 loop, the exprSrc/syntaxSrc
-- precedent) so the `{$ref}` field handles resolve in the catalog. `SetExpr.SeCtor
-- : List SetCtorField` and `SetCtorField.set : SetExpr` are the SAME mutual-
-- recursion idiom (decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1a) — SetCtorField registers in the
-- same pass.
-- =========================================================================

@entity
@label "SetExpr"
@description "A set expression — the constraint-AND-value language for any scalar field. 15 cases: SeAll / SeNone (the bounds), SeEnum (finite value set) / SeInterval (ordered range) / SeRef (name-handle, codeable-name or UUID) / SePattern (algebraic regex over sequences, mutually recursive with SetPattern) / SeWhere (JSON-Logic predicate) / SeCtor (the datatype constructor set — a variant is a SeUnion of its SeCtors, a record is a single SeCtor; the polynomial-functor building block, the 6D dt* term-theory's set-side mirror — decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1a) / SeMu (the fixpoint former μX.F — the bound occurrence rides SeRef {handle=var}; recursive-type denotations, decide-substrate Phase 8μ.1b) / SeArrow (the intensional function-signature set — params contravariant, returns covariant; membership by signature/type, never extensional; the exponential former, decide-substrate Phase 8λ.1) / SeRigid (the VALIDATION-ONLY rigid atom κ — signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a; minted only inside a validation frame, no $-key spelling, no named membership, no catalog resolver, no μ-binding, and an exhaustive decider matrix whose only Just true rows are κ⊆κ, ∅⊆κ, κ⊆⊤) — the leaves — and SeUnion / SeIntersect / SeDiff / SeComplement — the boolean combinators. The canonical registered SetExpr value; legacy $-key input exists only at the host boundary."
SetExpr =
  SeAll
  | SeNone
  | SeEnum values: List Any
  -- The host-canonical interval payload is deliberately structural and
  -- untagged.  SetInterval/SetBound below remain registered construction
  -- types, but are not the runtime carrier nested under SeInterval.
  | SeInterval interval: { lo: Maybe ({ value: Any, inclusive: Boolean }), hi: Maybe ({ value: Any, inclusive: Boolean }) }
  | SeRef handle: String
  | SePattern pattern: SetPattern
  | SeWhere pred: Any
  | SeCtor ctor: String fields: List SetCtorField
  | SeMu var: String body: SetExpr
  | SeArrow params: List SetArrowParam returns: SetExpr
  -- signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the VALIDATION-ONLY rigid atom κ.
  -- `scopeToken` is the scope-unique opaque mint nonce, `ordinal` the binder's
  -- position in the effective scheme's quantifier order, `kind` the binder's
  -- kind (KType / a fully applied KArrow — carried as Any because the kind
  -- vocabulary lives in the signature layer, not the set layer).
  --
  -- A rigid is NEVER encoded as SeMu: `μκ.κ` collapses to ⊥ (setAlgebraMuEmpty
  -- substitutes the bound var with SeNone, so `empty(μκ.κ) = Just true`), which
  -- would make every `∀a. a -> R` body validate vacuously.  It is its own
  -- constructor with NO arms rather than a reserved SeRef namespace precisely
  -- because the PUBLIC `registerNamedSet` accepts arbitrary handles, so a
  -- reserved-name rigid is capturable from outside the validation frame.
  --
  -- NON-ESCAPE is ASYMMETRIC (set-marker.ts; ledger rows rig.escape /
  -- rig.provenance / rig.kind): SeRigid IS in the host `SET_EXPR_TAGS` roster
  -- (excluding it made every host boundary silently reclassify a rigid as
  -- "not a SetExpr"), `peelSetExpr` recognizes one ONLY with a well-formed
  -- closed Kind, ingress `setExprToTag` THROWS unless an engine-internal
  -- decider seam passes `admitValidationRigid: true`, and the `$`-key egress
  -- `setExprToDollarKey` rejects a rigid at any recognized SetExpr child depth
  -- (opaque payloads are copied, not walked).  The only projection
  -- that may leave a validation frame is the `fenel.validation.rigid.v1`
  -- alpha-normalized digest.
  | SeRigid scopeToken: String ordinal: Nat kind: Any
  | SeUnion branches: List SetExpr
  | SeIntersect branches: List SetExpr
  | SeDiff left: SetExpr right: SetExpr
  | SeComplement inner: SetExpr

@entity
@label "SetPattern"
@description "An algebraic pattern (regex over sequences of values) — Brzozowski-derivative-friendly, mutually recursive with SetExpr. 7 cases: SpEmpty (matches nothing) / SpEps (matches the empty sequence) / SpMatch (one element satisfying a SetExpr predicate) / SpSeq (concatenation) / SpAlt (alternation) / SpRep (bounded repetition, min..max) / SpGroup (named typed capture — the captured subsequence must additionally satisfy the optional SetExpr). The Sp* namespace keeps this registered set-pattern vocabulary distinct from pattern-algebra's Pat P* constructors."
SetPattern =
  SpEmpty
  | SpEps
  | SpMatch pred: SetExpr
  | SpSeq a: SetPattern b: SetPattern
  | SpAlt a: SetPattern b: SetPattern
  | SpRep child: SetPattern min: Number max: Number
  | SpGroup name: String child: SetPattern type: Maybe SetExpr

@entity
@label "SetBoundValue"
@description "The value carried by an interval boundary — mirrors the TS `number | string | { $expr: Expression }` union. BvNumber / BvString are the literal forms; BvExpr carries a JSON-Logic expression (explicit Any carrier, per D3 — $where/$expr stay JSON-Logic, not the Expr ADT)."
SetBoundValue =
  BvNumber value: Number
  | BvString value: String
  | BvExpr expr: Any

@entity
@label "SetBound"
@description "An interval boundary — a SetBoundValue plus inclusivity. Single-constructor record (ctor name = type name) to keep the constructor namespace clear of the deciders' marshalled Bound."
SetBound = SetBound value: SetBoundValue inclusive: Boolean

@entity
@label "SetInterval"
@description "An interval on an ordered type — Nothing on lo/hi means unbounded in that direction. Single-constructor record (ctor name = type name) to keep the constructor namespace clear of the deciders' marshalled Interval."
SetInterval = SetInterval lo: Maybe SetBound hi: Maybe SetBound

@entity
@label "SetCtorField"
@description "One identity-total field of a SeCtor constructor set (field-identity Phase 3). `key` is the semantic axis (UUID-backed NamedField or ordinal PositionalField); `wireName` is only the current source/JSON/object-property projection; `set` is the value constraint. Constructor equality/subset/disjointness pair by key, while membership reads the host object by wireName. Mutually recursive with SetExpr via `.set`."
SetCtorField = SetCtorField key: FieldKey wireName: String set: SetExpr

@entity
@label "SetArrowParam"
@description "One identity-bearing parameter of a SeArrow signature (field-identity Phase 3). `key` and `wireName` survive for reflection and final emission, but arity and variance pair parameters strictly by list position; keys never reorder an arrow. Positional keys must agree with their local list ordinal. Mutually recursive with SetExpr via `.set`."
SetArrowParam = SetArrowParam key: FieldKey wireName: String set: SetExpr
